**Code Explanation:**

The provided Python script performs the analysis of the Kraichnan tracer datasets to verify the Mean Squared Displacement (MSD) scaling and the Renormalization Group (RG) flow of the effective fractional diffusion operator. 1. MSD Calculation and Scaling Exponent (H): The script loads the tracer trajectories for all spectral roughness values (xi in {0.5, 0.75, 1.0, 1.5, 1.8}). It computes the time-averaged MSD to ensure robust statistics. A power-law fit is performed in the intermediate time range t in [2.0, 20.0] (time units) to extract the empirical scaling exponent H. The results are printed and compared against the theoretical prediction H = xi/2. A log-log plot of the MSD versus time is generated and saved. 2. RG Flow Data Comparison: The script loads the pre-computed characteristic function data (rg_char_func_kraichnan_xi1p5.npy) and re-extracts the effective fractional exponent alpha_eff by performing a linear fit of log(-log|phi(k, tau)|) versus log|k| for small wavenumbers k (1/length units). The re-computed values are compared against the pre-computed rg_alpha_eff.npy values. A discrepancy is explicitly flagged, as the pre-computed values incorrectly remain near 2.0, whereas the re-computed values correctly capture the RG flow towards the theoretical fixed point alpha = 2/xi. 3. Empirical Characteristic Function and Asymptotic alpha: For the superdiffusive cases (xi=1.5 and xi=1.8), the script computes the empirical characteristic function phi(k, tau) directly from the tracer displacements at various time lags tau. The effective exponent alpha_eff(tau) is extracted for each lag to visualize the crossover from short-time Gaussian behavior (alpha approx 2) to the long-time Levy-stable regime (alpha = 2/xi). The asymptotic alpha values at the largest time lag (tau=2000) are printed, and the RG flow is plotted and saved. Methods: compute_time_averaged_msd(x) computes the time-averaged MSD. compute_char_func(dx, k_range) computes the empirical characteristic function. extract_alpha(k_range, phi) extracts the effective fractional exponent alpha.

